{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The land of the rising sun. It lived up to every expectation and then some! Just back from a whirlwind 10-day trip, and my head is still spinning with vibrant sights, delicious food, and unparalleled politeness.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a dazzling metropolis where ancient temples nestle between neon-lit skyscrapers. I spent hours wandering through Shibuya Crossing, marveling at the organized chaos, and finding tranquility in the Meiji Jingu Shrine. The food scene was incredible – from Michelin-starred restaurants to tiny ramen shops tucked away in alleyways, every meal was an adventure.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan.  Exploring Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates was breathtaking.  I also loved the Gion district, hoping for a glimpse of a geisha.  \n\nBeyond the big cities, I ventured to Hakone, a mountain resort town known for its stunning views of Mount Fuji.  Cruising across Lake Ashi with Fuji in the background was a truly unforgettable experience.\n\nThe people were incredibly helpful, even with my limited Japanese.  I learned a few basic phrases (\"arigato\" goes a long way!), and embraced the cultural differences.  \n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – tradition and modernity, bustling cities and serene landscapes. It's a place that stimulates all the senses and leaves you wanting more. I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0011703077470883727}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968507617712021}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.0798321068286895